   ],
   "key": "p14-2d221de7"
  },
  {
   "id": "p14-out-e18",
   "page": 14,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Yes",
   "bbox": [
    398.2,
    409.7,
    410.1,
    419.9
   ],
   "key": "p14-40185850"
  },
  {
   "id": "p14-out-e19",
   "page": 14,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "No • If isolated rash (raised, red rash in patient who is otherwise well without other symptoms): - Monitor for other symptoms for at least 30 minutes to pick up any other symptoms:",
   "bbox": [
    448.1,
    410.9,
    774.2,
    441.1
   ],
   "key": "p14-6f74d063"
  },
  {
   "id": "p14-out-e20",
   "page": 14,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "• If no other associated symptoms and patient remains well, pseudoallergic self-limiting rash likely: reassure patient and advise to take oral antihistamines. • Advise to seek urgent health care if any of the following develop: swelling of face, lips or tongue, difficulty breathing, abdominal pain, nausea or vomiting. • If other symptoms: discuss with doctor/specialist urgently. • If in doubt, treat as anaphylaxis 28.",
   "bbox": [
    448.1,
    440.1,
    789.2,
    501.1
   ],
   "key": "p14-ca11a418"
  },
  {
   "id": "p14-out-e21",
   "page": 14,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "No. Does patient have generalised urticaria (raised red rash/hives) involving the whole body?",
   "bbox": [
    393.0,
    355.7,
    732.6,
    365.9
   ],
   "key": "p14-1da3ff6f"
  },
  {
   "id": "p14-out-e22",
   "page": 14,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "No. Are signs or symptoms serious or life-threatening, even if only single body system (hypotension,",
   "bbox": [
    411.3,
    378.3,
    778.5,
    388.5
   ],
   "key": "p14-6178c72d"
  },
  {
   "id": "p14-out-e23",
   "page": 14,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "respiratory distress, or significant swelling of the tongue or lips)?",
   "bbox": [
    476.6,
    388.3,
    711.3,
    398.5
   ],
   "key": "p14-2211c9d1"
  },
  {
   "id": "p14-out-e24",
   "page": 14,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Decide when to treat for anaphylaxis Are 2 or more body systems involved?",
   "bbox": [
    462.0,
    323.1,
    603.2,
    343.3
   ],
   "key": "p14-0e16ed46"
  },
  {
   "id": "p14-out-e25",
   "page": 14,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Report adverse events following vaccinations Report electronically using the Med Safety app (scan the QR code for download) or complete Case Reporting Form (CRF)1 for Adverse Events Following Immunisation (AEFI) and forward to AEFI@health.gov.za.",
   "bbox": [
